
[1mUser Commands[0m

Usage: tacctl user <subcommand> [arguments]

Subcommands:
  [1mlist[0m                                         List all users (name, group, status, pw age, scopes)
  [1mshow[0m [0;36m<username>[0m                              Show user details incl. scope membership
  [1madd[0m [0;36m<username>[0m [0;36m<group>[0m                       Add a new user; lands in default scope
  [1madd[0m [0;36m<username>[0m [0;36m<group>[0m [0;36m--scopes <s>[0m[,s...]   Grant specific scopes at creation
  [1madd[0m [0;36m<username>[0m [0;36m<group>[0m [0;36m--hash <hash>[0m         Add with pre-generated bcrypt hash ([0;36m-[0m reads it from stdin)
  [1madd[0m [0;36m<username>[0m [0;36m<group>[0m [0;36m--no-change-required[0m  Skip the required password change (a new user must change it first)
  [1mremove[0m [0;36m<username>[0m                            Remove a user
  [1mpasswd[0m [0;36m<username>[0m                            Change a user's password
  [1mpasswd[0m [0;36m<username>[0m [0;36m--hash <hash>[0m              Change with pre-generated bcrypt hash ([0;36m-[0m reads it from stdin)
  [1mpasswd[0m [0;36m<username>[0m [0;36m--no-change-required[0m       Skip the required password change (a reset requires one)
  [1mdisable[0m [0;36m<username>[0m                           Disable a user (preserves hash)
  [1menable[0m [0;36m<username>[0m                            Re-enable a disabled user
  [1mrename[0m [0;36m<old>[0m [0;36m<new>[0m                           Rename a user
  [1mmove[0m [0;36m<user>[0m [0;36m<group>[0m                          Move user to a different group
  [1mverify[0m [0;36m<username>[0m                            Verify password and show user details
  [1mrequire-password-change[0m [0;36m<user>[0m [on|off]      Require, or lift, a password change at the next login
  [1mrequire-password-change[0m [0;36m--all[0m [on|off]       Require, or lift, it for every user (superusers are skipped)
  [1mscope[0m [0;36m<user>[0m list|add|remove|replace         Manage which scopes the user can auth from
  [1mscope[0m [0;36m<user>[0m remove [0;36m--all[0m                    Remove every scope from the user

Names: letters, digits, '_', '-' and '.', new ones in lower case; a '.' is never first, last or next to another.

Examples:
  tacctl user list
  tacctl user add jsmith superuser
  tacctl user add jsmith superuser --scopes prod,lab
  tacctl user scope jsmith add prod
  tacctl user verify jsmith

